-- A contrast, not a reading of item 6: the dispatch is forbidden only when a
-- completion receipt is present. PRESENT is always defined, so a missing
-- receipt makes the condition false and the monitor allows the dispatch.
-- Item 6 of openid/authzen#795 (as read on 2026-11-12) says that the absence
-- of a completion receipt is not confirmation that an earlier attempt did not
-- execute; this specification reads it as if it were. PRESENT is not
-- monotone (T3_present_not_monotone, formal/core/TRIEL_Core.thy): a late
-- recovery receipt turns an ALLOW given on less data into a condition that
-- is true.
--
-- completion_receipt is present, and true, exactly when prior_completed is
-- true in the companion scenario of specs/dispatch_rule.triel (MAPPING.md,
-- decision 1); otherwise it is absent.
--
-- The invariant is required by the grammar and takes no part in the
-- comparison.

SPECIFICATION authzen795_absence_check VERSION 1.0.0
    PROVENANCE_REQUIRED: true

SUBJECTS {
  pep      : SYSTEM,
  provider : ORACLE
}

TERMS {
  pep MUST_NOT dispatch WHEN PRESENT(completion_receipt)
}

FACTORS {
  completion_receipt : Boolean METADATA SOURCE provider
}

INVARIANTS {
  receipt_known : SAFETY : ALWAYS(completion_receipt == completion_receipt)
}
